# torch is a transitive dep (via sentence-transformers / langchain-huggingface
# for the BGE reranker). Deploy target is CPU-only Cloud Run (see
# terraform/main.tf OMP_NUM_THREADS tuning) — no GPU ever available. PyPI's
# default Linux torch wheel pulls in the full CUDA toolkit (~GBs, unused).
# This extra index publishes CPU-only builds (local version suffix `+cpu`,
# which PEP 440 ranks higher than the plain version) so the resolver picks
# the CUDA-free build instead.
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
# Explicit +cpu pin: with both indexes visible, pip's resolver does not
# automatically prefer the local-version CPU build over PyPI's default
# (CUDA-pulling) build, so the version has to be forced here.
torch==2.12.1+cpu

